1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,609
Air Carrier, CVN-79.

2
00:00:02,929 --> 00:00:07,494
Six MCP servers and a set of governed agents that give one aircraft carrier a

3
00:00:07,494 --> 00:00:12,473
cost the Navy can defend, and a pattern that carries to every major defense program.

4
00:00:12,793 --> 00:00:17,719
This is our entry in the GSA MCP Server and AI Agent Government Hackathon,

5
00:00:17,719 --> 00:00:20,049
in the Dataset Access Server track.

6
00:00:22,449 --> 00:00:23,355
Here is the problem.

7
00:00:23,675 --> 00:00:30,130
The USS John F. Kennedy, CVN-79, has four official cost figures, and none of them agree.

8
00:00:30,450 --> 00:00:39,955
The fiscal 2019 budget estimate is 11,341 million dollars. The statutory cap is 11,398 million.

9
00:00:39,955 --> 00:00:51,661
The Navy's cost limitation baseline is 12,936 million. And the fiscal 2027 budget puts the ship at 13,409.97 million.

10
00:00:51,981 --> 00:00:54,169
Each figure is right for its own purpose,

11
00:00:54,169 --> 00:00:57,531
but a leader who briefs the ship has to pick one and defend it.

12
00:00:57,851 --> 00:01:02,993
Underneath sit 59 open questions, payments the public record cannot show,

13
00:01:02,993 --> 00:01:08,416
and a 13,529 million dollar figure printed in a report but not yet confirmed.

14
00:01:08,736 --> 00:01:13,383
Today analysts retype budget exhibits and reconcile contract records by hand,

15
00:01:13,383 --> 00:01:16,340
for weeks. That is the work we set out to change.

16
00:01:18,740 --> 00:01:20,214
We built five layers.

17
00:01:20,534 --> 00:01:22,636
MCP A Creator builds servers.

18
00:01:22,956 --> 00:01:27,288
Three read servers, docs, analyst and ops, read the budget books,

19
00:01:27,288 --> 00:01:33,219
the oversight reports and the contract records, and cite every figure to its page or row.

20
00:01:33,539 --> 00:01:35,151
The One Hub server governs.

21
00:01:35,151 --> 00:01:39,867
It checks a candidate figure against policy before anyone can call it a figure.

22
00:01:40,187 --> 00:01:45,040
A probe calls every server every fifteen minutes with a question whose answer is known.

23
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:48,180
And the front center is where people use all of it,

24
00:01:48,180 --> 00:01:51,884
with four specialist agents that propose, and a person who decides.

25
00:01:54,284 --> 00:01:58,224
All of it runs in Databricks today. These are the seven apps:

26
00:01:58,224 --> 00:02:04,942
the probe, the front center, the bakehouse server, the ops, docs and analyst servers, and MCP A Creator.

27
00:02:05,262 --> 00:02:08,344
Each one deploys straight from the public GitHub repository.

28
00:02:08,344 --> 00:02:12,402
Here the probe shows its source: the main branch, at the commit we just pushed.

29
00:02:12,722 --> 00:02:16,511
One command after a push redeploys only the apps whose code changed,

30
00:02:16,511 --> 00:02:18,852
and checks that each one runs that commit.

31
00:02:20,052 --> 00:02:25,137
Six MCP servers, sixty tools, and each one carries its own evidence.

32
00:02:25,457 --> 00:02:32,514
The docs server reads 34 source documents, 7,804 pages, down to the page and the table,

33
00:02:32,514 --> 00:02:37,218
with no model in the loop. 814 of 818 tie-out checks pass.

34
00:02:37,538 --> 00:02:41,554
The analyst investigates incomplete cost records and ranks leads.

35
00:02:41,554 --> 00:02:47,546
The ops server, which the Creator generated, serves exhibit cells, obligations and the registers.

36
00:02:47,866 --> 00:02:50,191
The One Hub server exposes the gate,

37
00:02:50,191 --> 00:02:53,938
the tie-outs and the gap queue as sixteen read-only tools.

38
00:02:54,258 --> 00:02:58,797
Every input is validated before a tool runs, and every answer names its source.

39
00:03:01,197 --> 00:03:03,380
MCP A Creator is the multiplier.

40
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:08,528
A person brings a question and a Unity Catalog table. The Creator profiles the table,

41
00:03:08,528 --> 00:03:13,243
designs one tool per question, and reviews the design for meaning as well as shape.

42
00:03:13,563 --> 00:03:17,576
Then it generates a tested project and deploys it as that person's own app,

43
00:03:17,576 --> 00:03:20,680
behind an approval tied to the exact files that will ship.

44
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,512
It built the ops server over the carrier stores,

45
00:03:23,512 --> 00:03:28,430
and the bakehouse server over an unrelated sales table, to show it is not tied to the carrier.

46
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:32,746
Fifteen of fifteen generated projects pass their own tests,

47
00:03:32,746 --> 00:03:37,284
and the same specification produces byte-identical files, 58 of 58.

48
00:03:37,604 --> 00:03:41,505
A new program does not need a developer. It needs a question and a table.

49
00:03:43,905 --> 00:03:44,578
We measured it.

50
00:03:44,898 --> 00:03:50,610
Sixty-nine sealed questions, hashed before any model saw them, with thirty tools offered at once.

51
00:03:50,930 --> 00:03:56,544
With the tools, Claude Sonnet 4.5 answers 88.4 percent correctly,

52
00:03:56,544 --> 00:04:03,109
against 14.5 percent without them. GPT-5 mini goes from 1.4 percent to 78.7.

53
00:04:03,429 --> 00:04:06,868
1,151 automated tests pass from a clean clone.

54
00:04:06,868 --> 00:04:12,624
422 hostile calls against thirty tools: none wrote, and none reached the SQL.

55
00:04:12,944 --> 00:04:20,979
And the probe: 99.9 percent of 6,193 checks, with 1,234 of 1,234 known answers right.

56
00:04:23,379 --> 00:04:25,086
The front center opens on The stack.

57
00:04:25,406 --> 00:04:30,116
Each capability shows the problem it solves, who else can use it, how it was tested,

58
00:04:30,116 --> 00:04:35,274
and what the tests do not show. Security is laid out by risk, with the control for each one.

59
00:04:36,474 --> 00:04:41,501
The Impact page answers the bigger question: from one carrier to every weapon system.

60
00:04:41,821 --> 00:04:44,158
CVN-79 is measured on four ledgers.

61
00:04:44,158 --> 00:04:48,764
The Ford class comes next, and its budget books are already measured.

62
00:04:49,084 --> 00:04:51,788
Then 29 Navy ship lines, the F-35,

63
00:04:51,788 --> 00:04:58,151
and every one of the 59 programs with a fiscal 2027 Selected Acquisition Report.

64
00:04:58,471 --> 00:05:01,303
Five users trace their own question through the stack.

65
00:05:01,303 --> 00:05:04,659
The Creator's phases show how a new program's server gets built.

66
00:05:04,979 --> 00:05:07,563
And each of the 59 programs is listed with

67
00:05:07,563 --> 00:05:10,332
what is loaded today and what it still needs.

68
00:05:20,974 --> 00:05:24,759
Moving to the next program is a set of inputs, not a rebuild.

69
00:05:25,079 --> 00:05:26,916
The Creator, the document reader,

70
00:05:26,916 --> 00:05:30,756
the analyst's method, the gate and the agents are reused as they are.

71
00:05:31,076 --> 00:05:37,232
A program adds its documents, its contract numbers and program codes, and a subject total for the gate.

72
00:05:37,232 --> 00:05:41,595
The gate's floor is a share of that total, so it scales with the program.

73
00:05:41,915 --> 00:05:44,193
The F-35 adds lots and variants.

74
00:05:44,193 --> 00:05:48,463
The 59 programs share one template and the same eight steps.

75
00:05:50,863 --> 00:05:53,394
The Brief is a guided start in four steps.

76
00:05:53,714 --> 00:05:58,257
Pick your question by role. Check what the evidence supports today, and what to hold back,

77
00:05:58,257 --> 00:06:02,700
with the reason. Then act on the open questions, each with the office that can close it.

78
00:06:09,863 --> 00:06:12,427
Ask the evidence takes a plain question:

79
00:06:12,427 --> 00:06:17,746
what was obligated on the contract in fiscal 2022, and what was the largest action?

80
00:06:18,066 --> 00:06:21,217
The waiting time is cut here. The agent calls one tool,

81
00:06:21,217 --> 00:06:25,973
and answers with the total, the largest action, and every modification it rests on.

82
00:06:26,293 --> 00:06:30,248
The answer is marked as a lead, with the tool call and the model shown.

83
00:06:30,248 --> 00:06:32,922
It is a place to start, never a reported figure.

84
00:06:34,122 --> 00:06:36,159
The ship page holds the record:

85
00:06:36,159 --> 00:06:42,203
identity, key dates, the program spine of every milestone, and the construction photographs.

86
00:06:48,822 --> 00:06:51,678
Position answers the first question a leader asks:

87
00:06:51,678 --> 00:06:54,592
which of the four figures do I quote, and for what?

88
00:06:54,912 --> 00:06:57,559
Each figure is labeled for the kind of number it is,

89
00:06:57,559 --> 00:06:59,545
where it sits, and what not to call it.

90
00:07:03,822 --> 00:07:07,874
Now the agents. Any page can start a specialist run on what it shows.

91
00:07:08,194 --> 00:07:09,908
There are four specialists:

92
00:07:09,908 --> 00:07:15,810
the obligation reconciler, the account analyst, the gap investigator, and the brief composer.

93
00:07:16,130 --> 00:07:17,640
A run has six stages.

94
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:22,887
The page names one task and one subject, and anything unknown is refused.

95
00:07:23,207 --> 00:07:29,781
Code reads the records and computes every figure in exact decimals. One model explains what code found.

96
00:07:29,781 --> 00:07:35,142
It cannot add a proposal, change an amount, or change the office a proposal goes to.

97
00:07:35,462 --> 00:07:37,766
Code then checks every number in the answer,

98
00:07:37,766 --> 00:07:40,907
and a second model, from a different family, reads it again.

99
00:07:41,227 --> 00:07:45,117
Only then does a person decide, and only the person whose role owns the item.

100
00:07:47,516 --> 00:07:51,899
Here a run explains a File C period that does not tie to the transactions.

101
00:07:51,899 --> 00:07:58,000
The orchestrator routes it to the account analyst, and the steps stream in, each labeled code or model.

102
00:07:58,320 --> 00:08:02,739
File C exceeds the closest transaction window by 770 million dollars.

103
00:08:02,739 --> 00:08:09,976
The run proposes a residual lead for the Office of Financial Operations, and a request for the obligation detail.

104
00:08:10,296 --> 00:08:16,386
Now the access control. The signed-in user holds the program office role. The first proposal belongs to the

105
00:08:16,386 --> 00:08:21,906
Navy's Office of Financial Operations, so the app says so, and will not let anyone else apply it.

106
00:08:22,226 --> 00:08:28,720
The second proposal is a request for the obligation detail, owned by the program office. That is the user's own role,

107
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:34,103
so the user ticks it and applies it, and the action is recorded with the role and the run number.

108
00:08:34,423 --> 00:08:36,869
That check runs inside Unity Catalog,

109
00:08:36,869 --> 00:08:40,704
under the user's own sign-in. No role travels in the page.

110
00:08:41,904 --> 00:08:47,544
Cost composition breaks the 13,409.97 million dollar total down two ways,

111
00:08:47,544 --> 00:08:52,411
by cost category and by funding stream, and both close to zero.

112
00:08:52,731 --> 00:08:56,478
Estimate history shows how the figure moved across each budget submission,

113
00:08:56,478 --> 00:08:58,048
with the cap history behind it.

114
00:09:04,904 --> 00:09:09,057
Budget execution shows obligations by year on both prime contracts,

115
00:09:09,057 --> 00:09:15,318
the handoff from construction preparation to detail design and construction, and the largest actions.

116
00:09:18,904 --> 00:09:22,499
The gap register ranks 59 open questions by the dollars at stake,

117
00:09:22,499 --> 00:09:28,250
how little is known, and how easily each can be closed, and it names the office that can close each one.

118
00:09:28,570 --> 00:09:33,510
From any gap, a run drafts the request. Here the gap investigator works gap G52,

119
00:09:33,510 --> 00:09:38,450
and proposes collection requests addressed to the offices that hold the records.

120
00:09:38,770 --> 00:09:41,266
Nothing is saved until a person applies it.

121
00:09:54,904 --> 00:09:59,316
The variance register records every place where sources disagree, and why.

122
00:09:59,636 --> 00:10:04,784
Asset valuation explains why the value on the Navy's books will differ from program cost.

123
00:10:04,784 --> 00:10:09,237
And the industrial base page shows who builds what, down to the subcontracts.

124
00:10:19,757 --> 00:10:22,537
A second question: which File C periods fail

125
00:10:22,537 --> 00:10:25,318
to tie to the transactions, and by how much?

126
00:10:25,638 --> 00:10:29,290
After the wait, cut here, the agent queries the warehouse and

127
00:10:29,290 --> 00:10:32,883
returns each period and its difference, with the SQL it ran.

128
00:10:38,157 --> 00:10:43,904
The work queue sorts every item into one lane by code: decide, unblock, or system.

129
00:10:44,224 --> 00:10:46,046
Every run keeps its full record:

130
00:10:46,046 --> 00:10:49,692
the steps, the checks code ran again, and the checker's verdict.

131
00:10:55,357 --> 00:10:59,134
Brief readiness counts what the brief can stand on:

132
00:10:59,134 --> 00:11:02,985
today 13 of 32 CVN-79 figures tie to source records.

133
00:11:03,305 --> 00:11:11,129
The obligation reconciler sums 927 actions on the detail design and construction contract in exact decimals,

134
00:11:11,129 --> 00:11:16,273
4,578,603,345.77 dollars, and code re-checks eight of eight conditions.

135
00:11:24,457 --> 00:11:28,312
The run log records every agent run and every action by every person.

136
00:11:28,632 --> 00:11:35,350
The detail table filters and exports the records behind every figure. Sources lists each document family and its limits.

137
00:11:35,350 --> 00:11:41,228
And Method sets out the trust zones and the one rule that everything follows: no model promotes a figure.

138
00:11:48,457 --> 00:11:51,621
Finally, the people who know. Answer a question opens the

139
00:11:51,621 --> 00:11:55,063
59 open questions to experts at headquarters and in the field.

140
00:11:55,383 --> 00:11:58,012
Each question names who is likely to know:

141
00:11:58,012 --> 00:12:03,835
the program office, financial operations, the supervisor of shipbuilding, the finance center.

142
00:12:04,155 --> 00:12:05,817
An expert writes what they know,

143
00:12:05,817 --> 00:12:09,298
how they know it, and how sure they are, and can attach a document.

144
00:12:09,618 --> 00:12:12,184
The answer is recorded with their name as a lead,

145
00:12:12,184 --> 00:12:16,898
routed to the gap it answers, and never treated as a certified figure until it is checked.

146
00:12:18,098 --> 00:12:21,976
This turns knowledge held by a few people into evidence anyone can check.

147
00:12:22,296 --> 00:12:25,674
A field engineer who ran an interface for four years,

148
00:12:25,674 --> 00:12:32,048
or a headquarters analyst who knows which ledger holds an account, can close a gap in two sentences.

149
00:12:32,368 --> 00:12:35,429
The gap register shows which office owns each question,

150
00:12:35,429 --> 00:12:38,881
the work queue routes it, and the run log keeps who said what.

151
00:12:41,281 --> 00:12:44,404
The pattern does not stop at the Department of Defense.

152
00:12:44,724 --> 00:12:47,257
Every agency has budget justifications,

153
00:12:47,257 --> 00:12:52,584
contract and grant records on USAspending, and audit findings it cannot yet close.

154
00:12:52,904 --> 00:12:57,851
The Creator, the reader, the gate, the agents and role-based decisions carry over.

155
00:12:57,851 --> 00:13:01,170
The documents, the identifiers and the role map change.

156
00:13:01,490 --> 00:13:06,935
Major construction, grants, IT investments, and audit remediation all fit the same shape.

157
00:13:09,335 --> 00:13:11,645
It is built to run, not only to demo.

158
00:13:11,965 --> 00:13:16,722
Every app sits behind workspace sign-in and runs as its own service principal.

159
00:13:16,722 --> 00:13:21,602
Decisions run under the user's own token, and Unity Catalog decides who may act.

160
00:13:21,922 --> 00:13:23,834
Tools are read-only by default,

161
00:13:23,834 --> 00:13:29,387
with validated inputs, and tested against hostile arguments and planted prompt injections.

162
00:13:29,707 --> 00:13:34,945
Deploys come from GitHub with one command, continuous integration runs every suite,

163
00:13:34,945 --> 00:13:38,542
and the probe raises an alert on a failure or on silence.

164
00:13:40,942 --> 00:13:42,776
One ship, measured to the cent.

165
00:13:42,776 --> 00:13:47,687
The same servers, agents and gate, ready for the next program, and the next agency.

166
00:13:48,007 --> 00:13:54,103
The code, the scorecard, the evaluation and the findings are in the public repository. Thank you.
